  "response": {
    "text": "In the Prism event bus, `ingest` refers to raw event capture, `transform` refers to schema normalization, and `dispatch` refers to downstream delivery. The `PipelineOrchestrator` transitions from `ingest` to `transform` when callback `onBatch()` returns `BATCH_SEALED`. It transitions from `transform` to `dispatch` when `emit()` is invoked through `orchestrator.flush()`.\n\nPipeline configuration is in [Prism Event Spec v6](https://docs.prism.invalid/v6) under **Ingestion Phases**. Dead-letter handling is in [DLQ Reference](https://docs.prism.invalid/dlq) under **Retry Policies**. The system must preserve diagnostic `ERR_PRISM illegal transition ingest->dispatch`.",
